REPORT ZAB_09.
* Modularization Technique in ABAP.
* We have 2 types of MT -> 1(Source Code Modularizing) & 2(Functionality Modularizing).
* 1 -> Include and Macro's
* 2 -> Subroutine and Functiona Module.
*============================================================================================================
* #INCLUDE
* ZAB_INC1 , ZAB_INC2
*INCLUDE ZAB_INC2.
*
*Loop AT it_t001 into wa_t001.
*  WRITE:/ wa_t001-bukrs,
*          wa_t001-butxt,
*          wa_t001-ort01.
*ENDLOOP.
* We can't directly execute the include program. We need to execute it from the excutable program.
*============================================================================================================
*MACROS
* are used to perform arithmatical operations.
* Can take upto 9 Placeholders (&1 &2 &3 &4 ... &9)
*DATA R TYPE I.
*DEFINE ADDITION.
*  r = &1 + &2 .
*END-OF-DEFINITION.
*ADDITION 20 10.
*WRITE R.
*DATA RESULT TYPE I.
*DEFINE CAL.
*  RESULT = &1 &2 &3.
*END-OF-DEFINITION.
*CAL 10 * 2.
*WRITE RESULT.
*CAL 25 - 10.
*WRITE / RESULT.
** Manually filling the Internal table by using MACROS.
*TYPES : BEGIN OF TY_T001,
*        BUKRS TYPE T001-BUKRS,
*        BUTXT TYPE T001-BUTXT,
*        ORT01 TYPE T001-ORT01,
*        END OF TY_T001.
*
*DATA : WA_T001 TYPE TY_T001,
*       IT_T001 TYPE TABLE OF TY_T001.
*
*DEFINE FILL_TAB.
*  WA_T001-BUKRS = &1.
*  WA_T001-BUTXT = &2.
*  WA_T001-ORT01 = &3.
*  APPEND WA_T001 TO IT_T001.
*  CLEAR WA_T001.
*END-OF-DEFINITION.
*
*FILL_TAB '1000' 'TCS' 'HYD'.
*FILL_TAB '2000' 'HCL' 'MUM'.
*FILL_TAB '3000' 'IBM' 'CHE'.
*
*LOOP AT IT_T001 INTO WA_T001.
*  WRITE :/ WA_T001-BUKRS, WA_T001-BUTXT, WA_T001-ORT01.
*ENDLOOP.
*============================================================================================================
* SUB-ROUTINES
* Are procedure that we can define in any ABAP program & Calling from the same or some other Program.
* Procedure is the collection of the statements.
**Perform addition of 2 numbers by using subroutines.
*
*PARAMETER : P_INPUT1 TYPE I,
*            P_INPUT2 TYPE I.
*
*DATA R TYPE I.
*PERFORM ADDITION USING P_INPUT1 P_INPUT2 CHANGING R.
*FORM ADDITION USING A TYPE I B TYPE I CHANGING C TYPE I.
*  C = A + B.
*  WRITE C.
*ENDFORM.
* There are 2 types of subroutine.
* 1)Internal subroutine  2)External subroutine
* 1) Internal Subroutine -> Definition and Calling in the same Program.
* 2) External Subroutine -> Definition and calling in 2 different program.
* Based on the given company codes to display the company codes , company name , cities using subroutine.
*DATA V1 TYPE T001-BUKRS.
*
*SELECT-OPTIONS S_BUKRS FOR V1.
*
*TYPES : BEGIN OF TY_T001,
*          BUKRS TYPE T001-BUKRS,
*          BUTXT TYPE T001-BUTXT,
*          ORT01 TYPE T001-ORT01,
*        END OF TY_T001.
*
*DATA : WA_T001 TYPE TY_T001,
*       IT_T001 TYPE TABLE OF TY_T001.
*
*PERFORM GET_DATA.
*PERFORM DISPLAY_OUTPUT.
*
*FORM GET_DATA.
*  SELECT BUKRS BUTXT ORT01 FROM T001 INTO TABLE IT_T001 WHERE BUKRS IN S_BUKRS.
*ENDFORM.
*
*FORM DISPLAY_OUTPUT.
*  LOOP AT IT_T001 INTO WA_T001.
*    WRITE:/ WA_T001-BUKRS , WA_T001-BUTXT , WA_T001-ORT01.
*  ENDLOOP.
*ENDFORM.
